<title>JAPAN: Toyota says 100-110 yen appropriate dlr/yen level.</title>
<headline>Toyota says 100-110 yen appropriate dlr/yen level.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp said on Tuesday that an appropriate dollar-yen level would be 100-110 yen for exporters and importers.</p>
<p>Toyota also hopes to make its non-automobile business profitable by the year 2000, president Hiroshi Okusa told a news conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>If it is profitable at that time, Toyota may spin off its non-automobile units into independent firms or subsidiaries, he said.</p>
</text>
